The symlink itself is left in place (not silently replaced), the link target is not opened for writing, and no temp file is created: the refusal precedes the tmp path entirely.

--- dangling symlink variant (target does not exist) ---
$ rm lane-dangling/.ufo/evidence/round-96/c1/pins.json
$ ln -s /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r96/R96E3/does-not-exist.json lane-dangling/.ufo/evidence/round-96/c1/pins.json
$ ls -l lane-dangling/.ufo/evidence/round-96/c1/pins.json
lrwxrwxrwx 1 vgpnk vgpnk 57 Nov  8 09:29 lane-dangling/.ufo/evidence/round-96/c1/pins.json -> /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r96/R96E3/does-not-exist.json
$ cd lane-dangling && python3 -I .ufo/evidence/round-96/c1/make-pins96.py --lane /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r96/R96E3/lane-dangling --rev be6c22b6d8a94f07eee6b0fa79edab7df228c0b0
PINS_SETUP pins-symlink-refused
exit=2
$ ls -l /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r96/R96E3/does-not-exist.json
ls: cannot access '/fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r96/R96E3/does-not-exist.json': No such file or directory

The guard is os.path.lexists(out) and os.path.islink(out) (lines 85-86), so a dangling link is refused too — an attacker cannot get the write path to create the target through a broken link.

--- source lines (make-pins96.py 83-86) ---
    out = os.path.join(lane, PINS_PATH)
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out), exist_ok=True)
    if os.path.lexists(out) and os.path.islink(out):
        print("PINS_SETUP pins-symlink-refused"); return 2

Contrast: round-95 make-pins95.py on the same attack opened the destination with plain open(out, "w") and overwrote the outside file (R96E3-before-witness.out).
